    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανα-φορά</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>referring, reference,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1130a29
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					1.2.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>reference</i> of a question to an assembly, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				3.33
			</span></i>; to the people, <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Rhet.,
			<i>repetition</i> of a word at the beginning of several clauses, <i><span class="en">
